\draw[->] (8b)--(9a);\n\t\t\\draw[->] (9b)--(dotsa);\n\t\t\\draw (1,1) circle (.4);\n\t\t\\end{tikzpicture}","source_block_sha256":"d6c31b5801ac361f65e5ff0398036a4392d668b681bfb2e3ec17da2aa0598bc5","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":50,"source_file_sha256":"e9a73caefcc496d7074251a3ac15f66fd577415bd3a531dd23f79375502ee0ed","stream_end":193477,"stream_start":192936}
{"accessible_name":"Definition of a Dedekind-infinite set","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":194113,"content_start":193874,"environment_id":"projected-env-000400","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-559aead08264d579","expr-559aead08264d579","expr-559aead08264d579","expr-4c83b7c72d282430","expr-e87e17fb60ea3e6b","expr-3bddde26f2fb0130"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/hilberts-hotel.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000400","formula_count":6,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002761","projected-formula-0002762","projected-formula-0002763","projected-formula-0002764","projected-formula-0002765","projected-formula-0002766"],"instance_id":"inst-00050","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:hilbert:defn:DedekindInfinite"],"line":60,"listen_text":"Definition. A set A is Dedekind infinite if and only if there is an injection from A into a proper subset of A. Equivalently, some o is in A and an injection f maps A to A while o is outside the range of f.","long_description":"A set is Dedekind infinite exactly when it injects into a proper subset of itself.","name":"defn","object_class":"definition","offset":2272,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"e3054e981f7f36858875e50593f34dd37bdaaab48c681c1e095415b63485a23e","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":257,"source_block_sha256":"db9dec5ca71ae33c269d279a8c00622752fa596f5fd34871f91bbfec787daddc","source_end_line":64,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/hilberts-hotel.tex","source_line":60,"source_offset":2272},"source_block":"\\begin{defn}\\ollabel{defn:DedekindInfinite}\nA set $A$ is \\emph{Dedekind infinite} iff there is !!a{injection}\nfrom~$A$ to a proper subset of~$A$. That is, there is some $o \\in A$\nand !!a{injection} $f \\colon A \\to A$ such that $o \\notin \\ran{f}$.\n\\end{defn}","source_block_sha256":"db9dec5ca71ae33c269d279a8c00622752fa596f5fd34871f91bbfec787daddc","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":64,"source_file_sha256":"e9a73caefcc496d7074251a3ac15f66fd577415bd3a531dd23f79375502ee0ed","stream_end":194123,"stream_start":193862}
{"accessible_name":"Definition of closure under a function","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":195799,"content_start":195566,"environment_id":"projected-env-000403","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-4b68ab3847feda7d","expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-cd2f0baff250163a","expr-65c74c15a686187b","expr-5078fd05812c1247"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-algebra.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000403","formula_count":6,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002775","projected-formula-0002776","projected-formula-0002777","projected-formula-0002778","projected-formula-0002779","projected-formula-0002780"],"instance_id":"inst-00051","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:dedekind:Closure"],"line":41,"listen_text":"Definition. A set X is f closed if and only if, for every x in X, f of x is in X. For any o, the closure of o under f is the intersection of all sets X that contain o and are f closed.","long_description":"Defines f-closed sets and the closure generated from o under f.","name":"defn","object_class":"definition","offset":1585,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"bc7ac8bdf6338e2afb965642d0dfd9380f043490128371ee4f47983c09ed0669","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":250,"source_block_sha256":"f5f550a410c3b785afb822e6a338e100fc21ff40cc9444ab028007fc9ee703ed","source_end_line":46,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-algebra.tex","source_line":41,"source_offset":1585},"source_block":"\\begin{defn}\\ollabel{Closure}\n\tFor any function $f$, the set $X$ is $f$-\\emph{closed} {iff}\n\t$(\\forall x \\in X)f(x) \\in X$. Now define, for any $o$:\n\t$$\\closureofunder{f}{o} = \\bigcap\\Setabs{X}{o \\in X\\text{ and }X\n\\text{ is $f$-closed}}$$\n\\end{defn}","source_block_sha256":"f5f550a410c3b785afb822e6a338e100fc21ff40cc9444ab028007fc9ee703ed","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":46,"source_file_sha256":"9cee716bb8cb3bfd507ed5c17bbd4477d05995af6f8f8d411087793bdaa86036","stream_end":195809,"stream_start":195554}
{"accessible_name":"Lemma on closure properties","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":196457,"content_start":196091,"environment_id":"projected-env-000405","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-4c83b7c72d282430","expr-80bdf62a5368e073","expr-80dbb42071375608","expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-4b68ab3847feda7d","expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-9eaa7ff2c67746f0","expr-c817427196db20fb"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-algebra.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000405","formula_count":9,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002787","projected-formula-0002788","projected-formula-0002789","projected-formula-0002790","projected-formula-0002791","projected-formula-0002792","projected-formula-0002793","projected-formula-0002794","projected-formula-0002795"],"instance_id":"inst-00051","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:dedekind:closureclosed","sfr:infinite:dedekind:closurehaselem","sfr:infinite:dedekind:closureproperties","sfr:infinite:dedekind:closuresmallest"],"line":53,"listen_text":"Lemma. For every function f and every o in A: first, o belongs to the closure of o under f; second, that closure is f closed; and third, if X is f closed and contains o, then the closure of o under f is a subset of X.","long_description":"The generated closure contains o, is f closed, and is contained in every f-closed set containing o.","name":"lem","object_class":"lemma","offset":2111,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"348e372a0c5a61b53d11c1274758735713383160f8d52c2274c3fff5ffd0113f","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":378,"source_block_sha256":"6a129bf88b0495a574b85da83c9cd47e08feac5e9d42e8e58513c87bf6d29663","source_end_line":61,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-algebra.tex","source_line":53,"source_offset":2111},"source_block":"\\begin{lem}\\ollabel{closureproperties}\n\tFor any function $f$ and any $o \\in A$:\n\t\\begin{enumerate}\n\t\t\\item\\ollabel{closurehaselem} $o \\in \\closureofunder{f}{o}$; and\n\t\t\\item\\ollabel{closureclosed} $\\closureofunder{f}{o}$ is $f$-closed; and\n\t\t\\item\\ollabel{closuresmallest} if $X$ is $f$-closed and $o \\in\n\t\tX$, then $\\closureofunder{f}{o} \\subseteq X$\n\t\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{lem}","source_block_sha256":"6a129bf88b0495a574b85da83c9cd47e08feac5e9d42e8e58513c87bf6d29663","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":61,"source_file_sha256":"9cee716bb8cb3bfd507ed5c17bbd4477d05995af6f8f8d411087793bdaa86036","stream_end":196466,"stream_start":196080}
{"accessible_name":"Definition of a Dedekind algebra","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":197559,"content_start":197240,"environment_id":"projected-env-000408","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-559aead08264d579","expr-e87e17fb60ea3e6b","expr-4c83b7c72d282430","expr-3bddde26f2fb0130","expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-2c4a2ca5d9c5c3ee"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-algebra.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000408","formula_count":6,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002813","projected-formula-0002814","projected-formula-0002815","projected-formula-0002816","projected-formula-0002817","projected-formula-0002818"],"instance_id":"inst-00051","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:dedekind:ded:closure","sfr:infinite:dedekind:ded:injection","sfr:infinite:dedekind:ded:proper"],"line":81,"listen_text":"Definition. A Dedekind algebra consists of a set A, a function f from A to A, and an element o in A, satisfying three conditions: o is outside the range of f; f is injective; and A is exactly the closure of o under f.","long_description":"A Dedekind algebra consists of a carrier, an injective self-map, and a starting element outside its range that generates the carrier.","name":"defn","object_class":"definition","offset":3259,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"8f107ae67ae5064ba3016aa4da4b58f6bcc881c31b9ccf8f4df81f9f2c2d51d0","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":333,"source_block_sha256":"3830ae7ad3470035c1227c676347fdbe891efcf09caca10ebb479e14dcf36ac5","source_end_line":89,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-algebra.tex","source_line":81,"source_offset":3259},"source_block":"\\begin{defn}\nA \\emph{Dedekind algebra} is a set $A$ together with a function $f\n\\colon A \\to A$ and some $o \\in A$  such that:\n\t\\begin{enumerate}\n\t\t\\item \\ollabel{ded:proper} $o \\notin \\ran{f}$\n\t\t\\item \\ollabel{ded:injection} $f$ is !!a{injection}\n\t\t\\item \\ollabel{ded:closure} $A = \\closureofunder{f}{o}$\n\t\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{defn}","source_block_sha256":"3830ae7ad3470035c1227c676347fdbe891efcf09caca10ebb479e14dcf36ac5","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":89,"source_file_sha256":"9cee716bb8cb3bfd507ed5c17bbd4477d05995af6f8f8d411087793bdaa86036","stream_end":197569,"stream_start":197228}
{"accessible_name":"Theorem producing a Dedekind algebra","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":198067,"content_start":197956,"environment_id":"projected-env-000409","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":[],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-algebra.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000409","formula_count":0,"formula_ids":[],"instance_id":"inst-00051","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:dedekind:thm:DedekindInfiniteAlgebra"],"line":98,"listen_text":"Theorem. If there is a Dedekind-infinite set, then there is a Dedekind algebra.","long_description":"The existence of a Dedekind-infinite set implies the existence of a Dedekind algebra.","name":"thm","object_class":"theorem","offset":3976,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"7e890a37c714dd36261b4885f37cce0a0bf7d69401c8fc45e3a731a6c6457eaf","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":129,"source_block_sha256":"4f2633042bb57608ebcae764da2757b7f877d14d26ee771eab3948cc19e3b9f0","source_end_line":100,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-algebra.tex","source_line":98,"source_offset":3976},"source_block":"\\begin{thm}\\ollabel{thm:DedekindInfiniteAlgebra}\nIf there is a Dedekind infinite set, then there is a Dedekind algebra.\n\\end{thm}","source_block_sha256":"4f2633042bb57608ebcae764da2757b7f877d14d26ee771eab3948cc19e3b9f0","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":100,"source_file_sha256":"9cee716bb8cb3bfd507ed5c17bbd4477d05995af6f8f8d411087793bdaa86036","stream_end":198076,"stream_start":197945}
{"accessible_name":"Arithmetical induction theorem for Dedekind algebras","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":199597,"content_start":199349,"environment_id":"projected-env-000412","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-f487d244814c26b3","expr-4b68ab3847feda7d","expr-9eaa7ff2c67746f0","expr-0875e62f4c3091dc","expr-39ed9ed5dd6f3c6b"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-induction.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000412","formula_count":5,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002848","projected-formula-0002849","projected-formula-0002850","projected-formula-0002851","projected-formula-0002852"],"instance_id":"inst-00052","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:induction:thm:dedinfiniteinduction"],"line":16,"listen_text":"Theorem, arithmetical induction. Let N, s, o form a Dedekind algebra. For any set X, if o is in X and every n in both N and X has s of n in X, then N is a subset of X.","long_description":"A subset containing o and closed under successors contains the whole Dedekind-algebra carrier.","name":"thm","object_class":"theorem","offset":478,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"f1fc3fccb57b395656565c0dc3c93de8cf27ffe871ccff715f5cb13f38991b36","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":263,"source_block_sha256":"6ab4d4c72a5dbd18e02246d123a4ac5de63bfaddfe7bdd85e3f32969ea991a4b","source_end_line":21,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-induction.tex","source_line":16,"source_offset":478},"source_block":"\\begin{thm}[Arithmetical induction]\\ollabel{thm:dedinfiniteinduction}\nLet $N, s, o$ comprise a Dedekind algebra. Then for any set $X$:  \n\t\\begin{center}\n\t\tif $o \\in X$ and $(\\forall {n} \\in N \\cap X){s}({n}) \\in X$, {then} $N \\subseteq X$.\n\t\\end{center}\n\\end{thm}","source_block_sha256":"6ab4d4c72a5dbd18e02246d123a4ac5de63bfaddfe7bdd85e3f32969ea991a4b","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":21,"source_file_sha256":"ea5f6c80d70abca6f5598de3e221c2f60524c40cbf533ae8a5336d5bb7186537","stream_end":199606,"stream_start":199338}
{"accessible_name":"Formula induction schema for Dedekind algebras","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":200508,"content_start":200238,"environment_id":"projected-env-000415","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-f487d244814c26b3","expr-4b7ce6b75f0ec36f","expr-91e914ebb438beb7","expr-f6ed9342c6673a6f","expr-d6327c286ec1e6e3"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-induction.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000415","formula_count":5,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002857","projected-formula-0002858","projected-formula-0002859","projected-formula-0002860","projected-formula-0002861"],"instance_id":"inst-00052","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:induction:natinductionschema"],"line":37,"listen_text":"Corollary. Let N, s, o form a Dedekind algebra. For any formula phi of x, possibly with parameters: if phi of o holds and, for every n in N, phi of n implies phi of s of n, then phi holds of every n in N.","long_description":"A property holding at o and preserved by s holds throughout N.","name":"cor","object_class":"corollary","offset":1367,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"79adf6a034462ccef69f6aa3bd5350648c9b0c527977c29854d6faef9cb0b8f8","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":283,"source_block_sha256":"e61ca61168e3166d792b4dec84c1863865cc737e09b69fa561c05f13d7262fcc","source_end_line":44,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-induction.tex","source_line":37,"source_offset":1367},"source_block":"\\begin{cor}\\ollabel{natinductionschema}\nLet $N, s, o$ comprise a Dedekind algebra. Then for any formula\n$\\phi(x)$, which may have parameters:\n\\begin{center}\n\tif $\\phi(o)$ and $(\\forall {n} \\in N)(\\phi(n)\\lif\n\t\\phi({s}({n})))$, {then} $(\\forall n \\in N)\\phi(n)$\n\\end{center}\n\\end{cor}","source_block_sha256":"e61ca61168e3166d792b4dec84c1863865cc737e09b69fa561c05f13d7262fcc","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":44,"source_file_sha256":"ea5f6c80d70abca6f5598de3e221c2f60524c40cbf533ae8a5336d5bb7186537","stream_end":200517,"stream_start":200227}
{"accessible_name":"Fully quantified induction schema with parameters","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":2,"content_end":201244,"content_start":201013,"environment_id":"projected-env-000417","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-421a2dc8ae2405e1"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-induction.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000417","formula_count":1,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002866"],"instance_id":"inst-00052","label_keys":[],"line":57,"listen_text":"Display. For every v sub one through v sub k: if phi of o, with those parameters, holds, and for every x in N, phi of x, with those parameters, implies phi of s of x, with those parameters, then for every x in N, phi of x, with those parameters, holds.","long_description":"The parameter version of the induction schema with all free variables universally quantified.","name":"align*","object_class":"display_math","offset":2139,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"6dc8ce85dfd6dd417b1ee0df08440bbd0833d5c772bc61c548d7b66d45a77aad","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":254,"source_block_sha256":"5921c5be45288dd92416473670c62de3f3d128c3da9e88d325cb3e40db8f6c9e","source_end_line":61,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-induction.tex","source_line":57,"source_offset":2139},"source_block":"\t\\begin{align*}\n\t\t\t\\forall v_1 \\ldots \\forall v_k((&\\phi(o, v_1,\\ldots, v_k) \\land {}\\\\\n\t\t\t&\t(\\forall x \\in N)(\\phi(x,v_1, \\ldots, v_k) \\lif \\phi(s(x), v_1,\\ldots, v_k))) \\lif {}\\\\\n\t\t\t&\\hspace{3em} (\\forall x \\in N)\\phi(x, v_1,\\ldots, v_k))\n\t\\end{align*}","source_block_sha256":"5921c5be45288dd92416473670c62de3f3d128c3da9e88d325cb3e40db8f6c9e","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":61,"source_file_sha256":"ea5f6c80d70abca6f5598de3e221c2f60524c40cbf533ae8a5336d5bb7186537","stream_end":201256,"stream_start":200999}
{"accessible_name":"Recursive clauses for arithmetic operations","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":202267,"content_start":202069,"environment_id":"projected-env-000418","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-ee66a80dc463d16e"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-induction.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000418","formula_count":1,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002868"],"instance_id":"inst-00052","label_keys":[],"line":76,"listen_text":"Display. Six recursive clauses: a plus o equals a; a times o equals o; a to the power o equals s of o; a plus s of b equals s of the sum a plus b; a times s of b equals a times b plus a; and a to the power s of b equals a to the power b times a.","long_description":"Six recursion equations for addition, multiplication, and exponentiation in a Dedekind algebra.","name":"align*","object_class":"display_math","offset":3195,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"a8e43134138bd045c0ed8129ba26f56f8435b958be34f3196dc93ebf16a1ba60","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":221,"source_block_sha256":"bebd50937200c4954ea2d0057dfad31f77e3d4b9184269824fecc55dfc5c6a72","source_end_line":79,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/dedekind-induction.tex","source_line":76,"source_offset":3195},"source_block":"\\begin{align*}\n\t{a} + {o} &= {a} & & & {a} \\times {o} &= {o} & & & {a}^{o} &= s(o)\\\\\n{a} + {s}({b}) &= {s}({a}+{b}) &&& {a} \\times {s}({b}) &= ({a}\\times {b}) + {a}  & & & {a}^{{s}({b})} &= {a}^{b} \\times {a}\n\\end{align*}","source_block_sha256":"bebd50937200c4954ea2d0057dfad31f77e3d4b9184269824fecc55dfc5c6a72","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":79,"source_file_sha256":"ea5f6c80d70abca6f5598de3e221c2f60524c40cbf533ae8a5336d5bb7186537","stream_end":202279,"stream_start":202055}
{"accessible_name":"Lemma on closure of a set under a function","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":209690,"content_start":209321,"environment_id":"projected-env-000422","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-df7e70e5021544f4","expr-66b0f93b823d692e","expr-59daf8be37c50480","expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-4b68ab3847feda7d","expr-252f10c83610ebca","expr-86c26e5d38ac0d18","expr-746737c6f70e80e0"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/card-sb.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000422","formula_count":9,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002895","projected-formula-0002896","projected-formula-0002897","projected-formula-0002898","projected-formula-0002899","projected-formula-0002900","projected-formula-0002901","projected-formula-0002902","projected-formula-0002903"],"instance_id":"inst-00054","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:card-sb:Closureclosed","sfr:infinite:card-sb:Closurehaselem","sfr:infinite:card-sb:Closureprops","sfr:infinite:card-sb:Closuresmallest"],"line":35,"listen_text":"Lemma. For every function f and set B: first, B is a subset of the closure of B under f; second, the closure is f closed; and third, if X is f closed and contains B, then the closure of B under f is a subset of X.","long_description":"The closure of B contains B, is f closed, and is the least f-closed superset of B.","name":"lem","object_class":"lemma","offset":1352,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"b5333b9bf3cd4a8adda12c95073314b1b8c86c05b21b75c0c5691f80ab69dd86","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":381,"source_block_sha256":"f411a256c71437227953699dae8dd223314a39c2eec1406cf9d2f330c8a79719","source_end_line":43,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/card-sb.tex","source_line":35,"source_offset":1352},"source_block":"\\begin{lem}\\ollabel{Closureprops}\n\tFor any function $f$, and any $B$:\n\t\\begin{enumerate}\n\t\t\\item\\ollabel{Closurehaselem} $B \\subseteq \\Closureofunder{f}{B}$; and\n\t\t\\item\\ollabel{Closureclosed} $\\Closureofunder{f}{B}$ is $f$-closed; and\n\t\t\\item\\ollabel{Closuresmallest} if $X$ is $f$-closed and $B\n\t\t\\subseteq X$, then $\\Closureofunder{f}{B} \\subseteq X$.\n\t\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{lem}","source_block_sha256":"f411a256c71437227953699dae8dd223314a39c2eec1406cf9d2f330c8a79719","source_correction_ids":[],"source_end_line":43,"source_file_sha256":"88534a3f2be736a704ab31343e45933edb9712fa5b4411eb102c0f4a12d656e9","stream_end":209699,"stream_start":209310}
{"accessible_name":"Sandwich proposition for equinumerous sets","authoring_provenance":"TR007_EXPLICIT_FORMAL_OBJECT_REVIEW","authoring_status":"PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ORDER_CONTINUOUS_LINEARIZATION","chapter_key":"sfr:infinite","column":1,"content_end":209974,"content_start":209869,"environment_id":"projected-env-000424","exercise_solution_policy":null,"exercise_solution_status":null,"expression_ids":["expr-d9423412c7568727","expr-b585d7fee001c730","expr-c3db0e0ad6ce4b77"],"file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/card-sb.tex","formal_object_id":"projected-env-000424","formula_count":3,"formula_ids":["projected-formula-0002904","projected-formula-0002905","projected-formula-0002906"],"instance_id":"inst-00054","label_keys":["sfr:infinite:card-sb:sbhelper"],"line":51,"listen_text":"Proposition. If A is a subset of B, B is a subset of C, and A is equinumerous with C, then A is equinumerous with B and B is equinumerous with C. The immutable source contains a malformed nested cardinal-equality macro; this reading states the intended conclusion.","long_description":"If A is contained in B, B is contained in C, and A is equinumerous with C, then all three sets are equinumerous.","name":"prop","object_class":"proposition","offset":1899,"part_key":"sfr","record_sha256":"9e6016e8e99f4c5633128951391388777bc83012487d805d91f246714b6fb667","reference_ids":[],"scope":"projected","source_binding":{"source_block_bytes":125,"source_block_sha256":"59cbe9d285b114105302e209d86fb7f311fef04073ba06550451b72123271326","source_end_line":53,"source_file":"content/sets-functions-relations/infinite/card-sb.tex","source_line":51,"source_offset":1899},"source_block":"\\begin{prop}\\ollabel{sbhelper}\nIf $A \\subseteq B \\subseteq C$ and $A \\approx C$, then $\\cardeq{\\cardeq{A}{B}}{C}$.\n\\end{prop}","source_block_sha256":"59cbe9d285b114105302e209d86fb7f311fef04073ba06550451b72123271326","source_correction_ids":["TR007-SOURCE-FORMULA-002"],"source_end_line":53,"source_file_sha256":"88534a3f2be736a704ab31343e45933edb9712fa5b4411eb102c0f4a12d656e9","stream_end":209984,"stream_start":209857}
